  "identifier": "totalsegmentator",
  "name": "TotalSegmentator",
  "description": "Automated segmentation tool for 100+ anatomical structures in CT and MRI scans — covering abdominal organs (liver, spleen, pancreas, kidneys), thoracic structures (lungs, heart, aorta), vertebrae, ribs, muscles, and vasculature. Built on nnU-Net, installable as a Python package with a simple one-line CLI. 40+ additional specialised task models available (some under academic/commercial licence). Used in clinical research workflows for large-scale cohort studies. Published in Radiology: Artificial Intelligence 2023 (CT) and Radiology 2024 (MRI). Apache-2.0, Python, 2.7k stars, 427 forks, v2.5.0 (January 2025). Developed at University Hospital Basel.",
  "url": "https://totalsegmentator.com/",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/wasserth/TotalSegmentator",
